# K01d witness (steps/k01-selector-identity-20261001.md §5), negative: the candidate's LAST
# occurrence of the name is a char while the requirement's is a size_t, so a Consumer that
# reads the bare `v\x` (which selects exactly that occurrence in the VALUE) must be refused --
# even though the same candidate's occurrence 0 is a size_t and reads fine
# (unit_occ_selector_ordinal_ok).  Both spellings name the requirement's single field, and that
# is the point: they part company only in the candidate.  Mirror of
# unit_occ_selector_first_refused, where the ORDINAL half was the bad one.
Model: (size_t: x 10U)
Cand: (size_t: x 10U; char: x 'q')
fn: rdLast (Model: v) int
    size_t: got
    got: v\x
    return: (cast: (int) (got))
end: rdLast
c: merge: Cand
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: rdLast(c); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
